      "side": 1,
      "message": "The thread record mixes the first comment\u0027s place with the latest comment\u0027s id.\n\nA thread whose root is on patch set 1 and whose latest reply is on patch set 2 builds `patch_set: 1` from `$t[0]` with `latest` pointing at the patch-set-2 comment (reproduced with the init query on a synthetic two-comment thread: `{number: 1, patch_set: 1, latest: \"bbbbbbbb_22222222\"}` where the latest lives on patch set 2). `reply` then posts `patchSet: 1` with `inReplyTo` naming that patch-set-2 comment, contradicting this skill\u0027s own rule that a reply goes on its parent comment\u0027s patch set, file and line and the post job\u0027s note that Gerrit takes a reply nowhere else.\n\nFix: record the latest comment\u0027s place, `patch_set: $l.patch_set, path: $l.path, line: $l.line`.",
